# Materials Project search and POSCAR download (crystod-search); testsuite section 48
# Needs a free Materials Project API key (https://next-gen.materialsproject.org/api):
#   export MP_API_KEY=<key>   or once   pmg config --add PMG_MAPI_KEY <key>
# Data: the Materials Project, CC BY 4.0. Cite A. Jain et al., APL Mater. 1, 011002 (2013),
# https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4812323

Files (not in the pip package)
------------------------------
The commands below read no input file: they need only the network and an API key.
The files listed here are not in the pip package (they stay in the CrystOD
development tree); the copy of this example made by "crystod-example 48" holds
this README alone.

mp_summary_Sr-Ti-O.json.gz        offline fixture of testsuite section 48 (17 kB)
POSCAR_Sr2TiO4_I4mmm_mp-5532      written by "crystod-search --get mp-5532": the conventional cell
PPOSCAR_Sr2TiO4_I4mmm_mp-5532     written by "crystod-search --get mp-5532 --cell primitive"
                                  (both from the live run of the sample below)
record_fixture.py                 re-records the fixture (needs the network and a key)

The fixture holds Materials Project summary documents, recorded on 2026-09-18 from
https://api.materialsproject.org/materials/summary/ (API version 0.87.3): every entry
of the chemical system Sr-Ti-O and of all its subsystems (O, Sr, Ti, O-Sr, O-Ti, Sr-Ti,
O-Sr-Ti; 216 current and 6 deprecated entries) with the fields crystod-search requests
(material_id, formula_pretty, symmetry, band_gap, energy_above_hull, nsites, theoretical)
and those the server filters on (elements, nelements, chemsys, formula_anonymous,
composition_reduced, is_stable, deprecated), in the order the API returns them unsorted.
The crystal structure is included for the ten entries the tests download: the five SrTiO3
polymorphs and the six experimentally observed Sr-Ti-O ternaries (mp-5229 is both).
Material IDs are kept in the alphabetical form the API returns (mp-aaaaahtd = mp-5229).

"python testsuite.py 48" serves this file from a local stub of the summary endpoint
(the same query parameters, _fields/_sort_fields/_limit/_skip paging, error bodies and
401 answers as the live API, checked against it on the recording date), so the section
runs without network access or an API key and never contacts the Materials Project.
With CRYSTOD_LIVE_MP=1 it adds one live search.

